{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794561645305,"sessionID":"ses_e2bccb336ffeW5nAknN29DOzXD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4359258002iSEAJqsx0l8I6O","sessionID":"ses_e2bccb336ffeW5nAknN29DOzXD","messageID":"msg_1d4357300001tocTUFlXaVSNeF","type":"tool","id":"call_f6f92d1caeb14c38b17b1f7b","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts","oldString":"// Invokes the brief renderer per runtime. The iter-4 7-axis adapter divergence\n// matrix was measured for Claude and OpenCode only, so every other runtime reads\n// `not-recorded` on each axis. An invented axis reading would pass for a measured\n// one, so a runtime nobody probed carries `not-recorded` rather than a guess.\n// Loads the matrix as a fixture and asserts non-zero signal counts per runtime.\n// Collector-shape coverage for spec_kit.advisor.recommendation_emitted_total is\n// kept separate from the renderer signal/noise boundary so metric emission is not\n// confused with render behavior.","newString":"// Invokes the brief renderer per runtime (the iteration measured Claude and OpenCode, and the rest read not-recorded),\n// loads the iter-4 7-axis adapter divergence matrix as a fixture, and\n// asserts non-zero signal counts per runtime. Collector-shape coverage for\n// spec_kit.advisor.recommendation_emitted_total is kept separate from the\n// renderer signal/noise boundary so metric emission is not confused with render behavior."},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts\n@@ -1,15 +1,12 @@\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n // MODULE: Hook Brief Signal/Noise Bench\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n-// Invokes the brief renderer per runtime. The iter-4 7-axis adapter divergence\n-// matrix was measured for Claude and OpenCode only, so every other runtime reads\n-// `not-recorded` on each axis. An invented axis reading would pass for a measured\n-// one, so a runtime nobody probed carries `not-recorded` rather than a guess.\n-// Loads the matrix as a fixture and asserts non-zero signal counts per runtime.\n-// Collector-shape coverage for spec_kit.advisor.recommendation_emitted_total is\n-// kept separate from the renderer signal/noise boundary so metric emission is not\n-// confused with render behavior.\n+// Invokes the brief renderer per runtime (the iteration measured Claude and OpenCode, and the rest read not-recorded),\n+// loads the iter-4 7-axis adapter divergence matrix as a fixture, and\n+// asserts non-zero signal counts per runtime. Collector-shape coverage for\n+// spec_kit.advisor.recommendation_emitted_total is kept separate from the\n+// renderer signal/noise boundary so metric emission is not confused with render behavior.\n \n import { describe, expect, it, beforeAll, afterAll } from 'vitest';\n import { renderAdvisorBrief } from '../lib/render.js';\n import {\n","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":8}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts\",\"oldString\":\"// Invokes the brief renderer per runtime. The iter-4 7-axis adapter divergence\\n// matrix was measured for Claude and OpenCode only, so every other runtime reads\\n// `not-recorded` on each axis. An invented axis reading would pass for a measured\\n// one, so a runtime nobody probed carries `not-recorded` rather than a guess.\\n// Loads the matrix as a fixture and asserts non-zero signal counts per runtime.\\n// Collector-shape coverage for spec_kit.advisor.recommendation_emitted_total is\\n// kept separate from the renderer signal/noise boundary so metric emission is not\\n// confused with render behavior.\",\"newString\":\"// Invokes the brief renderer per runtime (the iteration measured Claude and OpenCode, and the rest read not-recorded),\\n// loads the iter-4 7-axis adapter divergence matrix as a fixture, and\\n// asserts non-zero signal counts per runtime. Collector-shape coverage for\\n// spec_kit.advisor.recommendation_emitted_total is kept separate from the\\n// renderer signal/noise boundary so metric emission is not confused with render behavior.\"}"},"time":{"start":1794561643096,"end":1794561645305}}}}
